{
  "schema_version": 1,
  "id": "07-constructor-as-type-reference",
  "title": "Constructor as type reference: &models.Job{} is a scip_type_reference, not a call edge",
  "rule_pack": "rules-static-v1",
  "provenance": {
    "kind": "synthetic",
    "source": "hand-authored adversarial static case",
    "seeded_fault": null
  },
  "context": {
    "index": "43cd33501653a8f7fa035219834c9859d744cf7137a79db772cad9e54e402e3a"
  },
  "review_notes": [
    "Repo#Get constructs &models.Job{}; the indexer records scip_type_reference(Repo#Get, models/Job#) and no scip_may_reference to the type.",
    "The capability is supported through the op owner: static_site_owner attributes the gorm First on jobs to Repo#Get, which GetJob reaches.",
    "static_reaches(GetJob, models/Job#) is unresolved: reachability follows call edges only, and the type reference is not one. This is documented, not a defect."
  ],
